      "id": "new-york-holidays",
      "sourceUrl": "https://www.nysenate.gov/legislation/laws/GCN/24",
      "title": "The public holidays of New York (N.Y. Gen. Constr. Law § 24) that\n`us-federal-holidays` does not already close: Lincoln's birthday, February\n12 (the next day when it falls on a Sunday; a Saturday one is not moved),\nand each general election day, held every year on the Tuesday after the\nfirst Monday in November (Election Law § 8-100, not vendored), listed with\n`once` to the end of 2050. Flag day, the second Sunday in June, is closed by\n`weekend`. Closed from the date the vendored text was retrieved (October 29,\n2026; it carries no as-of date). Not modeled: the days the President or the\nGovernor appoints, which no vendored source lists."
    }
